.TH FEOF 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
feof \- test a Crunch stream's end-of-file indicator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "int feof(struct FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR feof ()
tests the stream's end-of-file indicator without changing it.
The indicator is set when a read encounters end-of-file, not merely when
the current position reaches the end.
It remains set until a successful
.BR fseek (3crunch),
.BR rewind (3crunch),
.BR clearerr (3crunch),
or until the stream is closed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns nonzero if the indicator is set and zero otherwise.
For a null stream, returns \-1 and sets
.B errno
to
.BR EINVAL ;
null is not a valid C stream argument.
Valid calls leave
.B errno
unchanged.
.SH NOTES
Only Crunch streams are supported; they are not C library
.B FILE
objects.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clearerr (3crunch),
.BR ferror (3crunch),
.BR fread (3crunch),
.BR fseek (3crunch)
